Silo patch 0018 — winecoreaudio: a game's sound follows the Mac's default output

Origin: camsteinberg/mavrik-engine `patches/0043-winecoreaudio-follow-the-default-output.patch` (version 2, Cam
Steinberg, Mavrik's own work, LGPL-2.1-or-later, at b018805, 2026-11-18). Its shape is upstream Wine's on Linux
(winepulse's "PulseAudio Output" and winealsa's `default`: a first endpoint that follows the system default) and
its mechanism OpenAL Soft's on the Mac (kAudioUnitSubType_DefaultOutput when no device is named); Mavrik copied no
code from either. Wine bugs 54779 and 55970 (open). Ported on 0017: 28 of 30 hunks apply as is; the two
rejected ones only change call sites (dev_id_from_device's new flow argument in unix_get_mix_format and
unix_is_format_supported, get_audiounit's new follow_default = FALSE in the latter), which differ in context
because our 0007 shortens get_mix_format and adds the SpatialMixer's mixer_unit; they were applied by hand.

Why: winecoreaudio bound each stream to the device that was the default when the stream was made (a
kAudioUnitSubType_HALOutput unit with CurrentDevice set). Connecting AirPods left the game on the speakers; a
device that went away (AirPods back in the case) left it silent until a restart. Now winecoreaudio lists
"System Default Output" (and "System Default Input") first, as the default endpoint, with an empty device string,
then every device as before. A render stream on it uses kAudioUnitSubType_DefaultOutput with no device set, so
macOS moves it to each new default output. A stream on a named device stays there, as on Windows. A listener on
the unit's current device gives each new device the stream's period as its I/O buffer, in device frames (0017).
"System Default Input" opens the default input of the moment and does not follow. mmdevapi is unchanged, so
OnDefaultDeviceChanged is not sent (as under winepulse).

Silo-specific: our 0007 adds a SpatialMixer when a stream has more channels than the device; that mixer is built
for the device the stream starts on, and after a move Apple's output unit converts its output to the new device.
Mavrik doesn't carry the SpatialMixer, so this combination was Silo's alone to verify.

Checked here: applies after 0002-0017 (with the two hand-applied call sites); coreaudio.c compiles with the
runtime's flags with no warning. On device (2026-11-22, user-verified, winecoreaudio.so with 0017+0018 swapped into
wine-cx-26.3.0): UNCHARTED: Legacy of Thieves Collection in "Automatico (Tradizionale)", its 7.1 stream through the
SpatialMixer, played clean on the MacBook speakers (48 kHz); taking the AirPods out moved the sound to them, and
putting them back in the case brought it back to the speakers, not silence.

